lls, expert ratings, or market pricing yet available, the race begins as a pure tossup.\n\nThe state's prominence in the 2028 Democratic primary calendar, including polling of prospective candidates and attention to its Senate and House contests, signals heavy investment ahead, but primary fights say little about the general election. Both parties can be expected to pour resources into Michigan, with turnout and persuasion in Detroit's suburbs and the industrial midlands likely to decide the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4963, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5203, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.4949, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4948, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4983, "margin": 0.0}]}